    "reviews": "\u201cIt's all wonderfully satisfying. Blocks of earth come apart in little bursts of pixels as you pepper them with sprays of bullets, something always seems to be exploding, and an ever depleting fuel meter gives the game a brilliantly frantic pace.\u201d<br>PC Gamer<br><br>\u201cThe sheer amount of quantified destruction on display is just, yep, that's the good stuff right there.\u201d<br>Rock Paper Shotgun<br><br>\u201cIncredibly hard to put down from the moment I tried it ... It's a dead-simple formula that got its hooks into my brain in approximately 11 seconds.\u201d<br>GamesRadar+<br>",
